<NPCCharacters>
  <!-- Fully independent Georgian (Culture.sturgia) troop tree - new character ids, own upgrade
       chain, own equipment loadouts. Does NOT reuse or touch Native's sturgian_*/varyag/druzhinnik
       troops (those stay exactly as Native shipped them; georgian_troops.xml's rename of them is
       now vestigial but harmless, kept for Custom Battle/tournament troop lists that still
       reference the native ids directly - same pattern as byzantine_troops.xml/abbasid_troops.xml).
       Every equipment item id below is a real, already-shipped Native item (verified against
       SandBoxCore/ModuleData/items/*.xml's own <Item>/<CraftedItem> definitions, excluding nested
       <Piece> crafting components which are not directly equippable).
       Tier structure (6/11/16/21/26/31) and per-tier skill-point totals (90/195/360/508/676/835)
       match this mod's own Khuzait-audited Seljuk tree and byzantine_custom_troops.xml's Byzantine
       tree exactly - each branch below reuses that same skill-point budget per tier so Georgia's
       tree is neither weaker nor stronger than its Byzantine/Abbasid counterparts.
       Historical grounding: Msakhuri (noble retainer-soldier), Aznauri (lesser/service nobility,
       light cavalry), Didebuli/Eristavi (great nobility/dukes, heavy cavalry), Khevsur and Svan
       (real highland warrior cultures of Georgia, famous for chainmail and close-quarters combat),
       Mtiuli (mountaineers, historically renowned hunters and archers), Alan (steppe people allied
       to and settled in the Caucasus, supplying horse-archers to Georgian kings - David IV's own
       reign, this mod's Georgian era, is when ~40,000 Kipchaks entered Georgian service), Monaspa
       (the historically attested royal bodyguard corps), Kartli and Sepe (the core Kingdom of
       Kartli region / "royal, of the crown" - used here as escalating unit-tier prefixes, mirroring
       how byzantine_custom_troops.xml escalates Skutatos through "Thematic"/"Tagmatic" prefixes). -->

